@startuml Chain of Responsibility Pattern - Commission Approval

' Define the styles (matching observer pattern style)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Chain of Responsibility Pattern - Commission Approval Workflow

' Request
class CommissionApprovalRequest <<Request>> {
  -requestId: String
  -deal: Deal
  -salesRepId: String
  -salesRepName: String
  -commissionAmount: BigDecimal
  -requestDate: LocalDate
  -approvalHistory: List<String>
  -approved: boolean
  -rejected: boolean
  -rejectionReason: String
  +approve(approver, comments): void
  +reject(rejector, reason): void
  +addToHistory(entry): void
  +isProcessed(): boolean
  +getCommissionAmount(): BigDecimal
}

' Handler Interface
interface ApprovalHandler <<Handler>> {
  +setNext(handler: ApprovalHandler): ApprovalHandler
  +approve(request: CommissionApprovalRequest): void
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

' Base Handler
abstract class BaseApprovalHandler <<BaseHandler>> {
  -nextHandler: ApprovalHandler
  +setNext(handler: ApprovalHandler): ApprovalHandler
  +approve(request: CommissionApprovalRequest): void
  #passToNext(request): void
  #{abstract} canApprove(request): boolean
  #{abstract} processApproval(request): void
  #shouldContinueChain(request): boolean
}

' Business Logic Handlers
class AutoApprovalHandler <<ConcreteHandler>> {
  -THRESHOLD: BigDecimal = 5000
  #canApprove(request): boolean
  #processApproval(request): void
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

class SalesManagerApprovalHandler <<ConcreteHandler>> {
  -MIN_THRESHOLD: BigDecimal = 5000
  -MAX_THRESHOLD: BigDecimal = 25000
  -managerName: String
  #canApprove(request): boolean
  #processApproval(request): void
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

class RegionalDirectorApprovalHandler <<ConcreteHandler>> {
  -MIN_THRESHOLD: BigDecimal = 25000
  -MAX_THRESHOLD: BigDecimal = 100000
  -directorName: String
  #canApprove(request): boolean
  #processApproval(request): void
  -hasValidDocumentation(request): boolean
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

class VPSalesApprovalHandler <<ConcreteHandler>> {
  -MIN_THRESHOLD: BigDecimal = 100000
  -MAX_THRESHOLD: BigDecimal = 500000
  -vpName: String
  #canApprove(request): boolean
  #processApproval(request): void
  -meetsExecutiveReviewCriteria(request): boolean
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

class CFOApprovalHandler <<ConcreteHandler>> {
  -THRESHOLD: BigDecimal = 500000
  -cfoName: String
  #canApprove(request): boolean
  #processApproval(request): void
  -meetsFinancialGuidelines(request): boolean
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

' Interceptor Handlers
class ValidationHandler <<Interceptor>> {
  #canApprove(request): boolean
  #processApproval(request): void
  #shouldContinueChain(request): boolean
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

class FraudDetectionHandler <<Interceptor>> {
  #canApprove(request): boolean
  #processApproval(request): void
  #shouldContinueChain(request): boolean
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

class AuditLogHandler <<Interceptor>> {
  #canApprove(request): boolean
  #processApproval(request): void
  #shouldContinueChain(request): boolean
  +getHandlerName(): String
}

' Domain Model
class Deal <<DomainModel>> {
  -id: String
  -title: String
  -value: BigDecimal
  -status: DealStatus
  -closeDate: LocalDate
}

' Relationships
ApprovalHandler <|.. BaseApprovalHandler
BaseApprovalHandler <|-- AutoApprovalHandler
BaseApprovalHandler <|-- SalesManagerApprovalHandler
BaseApprovalHandler <|-- RegionalDirectorApprovalHandler
BaseApprovalHandler <|-- VPSalesApprovalHandler
BaseApprovalHandler <|-- CFOApprovalHandler
BaseApprovalHandler <|-- ValidationHandler
BaseApprovalHandler <|-- FraudDetectionHandler
BaseApprovalHandler <|-- AuditLogHandler

BaseApprovalHandler o--> "0..1" ApprovalHandler : nextHandler

ApprovalHandler ..> CommissionApprovalRequest : processes >
CommissionApprovalRequest o--> Deal : references

' Chain flow (showing typical chain order)
ValidationHandler .right.> FraudDetectionHandler : setNext()
FraudDetectionHandler .right.> AutoApprovalHandler : setNext()
AutoApprovalHandler .down.> SalesManagerApprovalHandler : setNext()
SalesManagerApprovalHandler .down.> RegionalDirectorApprovalHandler : setNext()
RegionalDirectorApprovalHandler .down.> VPSalesApprovalHandler : setNext()
VPSalesApprovalHandler .down.> CFOApprovalHandler : setNext()
CFOApprovalHandler .down.> AuditLogHandler : setNext()

' Pattern component notes
note top of ApprovalHandler
  <b>Handler Interface</b>

  Defines the interface for handling requests.

  <b>Key methods:</b>
  • setNext() - builds the chain
  • approve() - processes request
  • getHandlerName() - for logging/debugging
end note

note right of BaseApprovalHandler
  <b>Base Handler</b>

  Provides chain management logic:
  • Maintains reference to next handler
  • Implements chain traversal
  • Template method for handling

  <b>Decision flow:</b>
  1. Can this handler process?
     → Yes: Process and maybe continue
     → No: Pass to next
  2. If processed, continue chain?
     → Yes: Call next handler
     → No: Stop chain
end note

note bottom of AutoApprovalHandler
  <b>Auto-Approval Handler</b>

  <b>Authority:</b> System
  <b>Range:</b> < $5,000

  <b>Logic:</b>
  Automatically approves low-value
  commissions without human approval.

  <b>Stops chain:</b> Yes (after approval)
end note

note bottom of SalesManagerApprovalHandler
  <b>Sales Manager Handler</b>

  <b>Authority:</b> Manager level
  <b>Range:</b> $5,000 - $25,000

  <b>Logic:</b>
  Validates deal status and approves
  within manager authority limit.

  <b>Stops chain:</b> Yes (after approval)
end note

note bottom of RegionalDirectorApprovalHandler
  <b>Regional Director Handler</b>

  <b>Authority:</b> Director level
  <b>Range:</b> $25,000 - $100,000

  <b>Logic:</b>
  Checks documentation and approves
  within director authority limit.

  <b>Stops chain:</b> Yes (after approval)
end note

note bottom of VPSalesApprovalHandler
  <b>VP of Sales Handler</b>

  <b>Authority:</b> Executive level
  <b>Range:</b> $100,000 - $500,000

  <b>Logic:</b>
  Executive review of commission
  rate and deal structure.

  <b>Stops chain:</b> Yes (after approval)
end note

note bottom of CFOApprovalHandler
  <b>CFO Handler</b>

  <b>Authority:</b> Highest level
  <b>Range:</b> ≥ $500,000

  <b>Logic:</b>
  Financial review for very large
  commissions. Ultimate authority.

  <b>Stops chain:</b> Yes (after approval)
end note

note left of ValidationHandler
  <b>Validation Interceptor</b>

  <b>Type:</b> Cross-cutting concern

  <b>Logic:</b>
  Validates all requests:
  • Positive amount
  • Deal is WON
  • Sales rep exists

  <b>Stops chain:</b> Only if invalid
  <b>Continues:</b> If valid
end note

note left of FraudDetectionHandler
  <b>Fraud Detection Interceptor</b>

  <b>Type:</b> Cross-cutting concern

  <b>Logic:</b>
  Checks fraud indicators:
  • Unusually high commission rate
  • Same-day deal close
  • Other suspicious patterns

  <b>Stops chain:</b> Only if fraud detected
  <b>Continues:</b> If clean
end note

note left of AuditLogHandler
  <b>Audit Log Interceptor</b>

  <b>Type:</b> Cross-cutting concern

  <b>Logic:</b>
  Records audit trail for all
  requests regardless of outcome.

  <b>Stops chain:</b> No (always continues)
  <b>Continues:</b> Always
end note

note bottom of CommissionApprovalRequest
  <b>Request Object</b>

  Contains all data needed for approval:
  • Deal information
  • Commission amount
  • Sales rep details
  • Approval history (audit trail)
  • Status (approved/rejected/pending)

  <b>Maintains state during chain traversal</b>
end note

' Chain flow diagram
note as N1
  <b>TYPICAL CHAIN FLOW</b>

  Request → Validation → Fraud Detection
    ↓
  If valid and clean:
    → Auto-Approval (< $5k) [STOP if approved]
    → Sales Manager ($5k-$25k) [STOP if approved]
    → Regional Director ($25k-$100k) [STOP if approved]
    → VP Sales ($100k-$500k) [STOP if approved]
    → CFO (≥ $500k) [STOP if approved]
    → Audit Log [Record trail]

  <b>Key Points:</b>
  • Interceptors run for ALL requests
  • Only ONE authority approves (stops chain)
  • Audit always runs (even if rejected)
  • History tracked throughout chain
end note

' Legend
legend right
  <b>Chain of Responsibility Pattern Components:</b>

  <b>Handler (Interface):</b> Defines handling interface
  and chain management methods.

  <b>BaseHandler (Abstract):</b> Implements chain logic
  and provides template for concrete handlers.

  <b>ConcreteHandler:</b> Implements specific handling
  logic. Decides if it can handle request.

  <b>Request:</b> Object containing data to be processed.
  Passed along the chain.

  <b>Handler Types:</b>
  1. <b>Business Logic Handlers:</b> Approval authorities
     (Auto, Manager, Director, VP, CFO)
     → Process and STOP chain

  2. <b>Interceptor Handlers:</b> Cross-cutting concerns
     (Validation, Fraud Detection, Audit)
     → Process and CONTINUE chain

  <b>Key Benefits:</b>
  ✓ Decouples sender from receiver
  ✓ Flexible chain composition
  ✓ Single responsibility per handler
  ✓ Easy to add/remove handlers
  ✓ Natural audit trail creation

  <b>Chain Building:</b>
  handler1.setNext(handler2)
         .setNext(handler3)
         .setNext(handler4);
endlegend

@enduml